comments.body:
@reporter So we have merged the PR https://github.com/Lightning-AI/lightning/pull/18049 to solve one of the problems you described (https://github.com/Lightning-AI/lightning/issues/18008#issuecomment-1626369069). You no longer have to do this and can just use `fabric.load_raw()` instead. [Documentation](https://lightning.ai/docs/fabric/latest/guide/checkpoint.html#from-a-raw-state-dict-file)

I will work on the more efficient data loading next to avoid the OOM.

Regarding your multi-node issues, I can't exactly pinpoint what could go wrong. It looks like your are using it correctly based on your description. We've been running multi-node experiments with an internal system (not using `lightning run model` though) and it is working without issues. How could I help you with this. Maybe we could jump on a call and pair-debug this?
